    rcap:evidenceSection "11.2" ;
    rcap:evidenceText "The occurrence of the following should be screened for and reported as SAEs for all patients in this domain, irrespective of intervention allocation: • Severe thrombocytopenia, out of keeping with clinical disease • Severe neutropenia, out of keeping with clinical disease • Increase in LFTs to 5x upper limit of normal • Gastrointestinal perforation Other SAEs should be reported only where, in the opinion of the site-investigator, the event might reasonably have occurred as a consequence of a study intervention or study participation (see relevant Core Protocol documents)." ;
